--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/5 + [expr.new]: a pack expansion in a
new-initializer's expression-list inside a FREE function template --
`::new((void*)__location) _Tp(forward<_Args>(__args)...)`, the C++20
std::construct_at body -- must replicate the pattern per pack element.
Was KNOWNBUG (>= 2 forwarded arguments dropped the body, "no body for
callee construct_at").  Fixed by adding a cpp_new-initializer branch to
the free-function-template body pack-expander in
cpp_instantiate_template.cpp, mirroring the existing function-call and
declarator-init_args branches.  Also required: void-returning constexpr
member function templates are now deferred rather than eagerly converted
([temp.inst]/5 -- a void call never yields a constant to fold), so the
allocator_traits::construct wrapper's body is expanded by the deferred
pass instead of failing an early eager conversion.  g++/clang++
runtime-verified.
